# ─── World ID (Developer Portal) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/03-worldid.md §2 — the action is the nullifier namespace, versioned.
# Changing it after launch resets every nullifier uniqueness guarantee. The vouch
# presence proof reuses THIS action (errata E-1) — nullifiers are unlinkable across
# actions, so a separate one could never be tied back to the enrolled human.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ID=app_staging_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# The RP ID is a SECOND, DIFFERENT value from the app ID — both are shown in the Developer
# Portal, and they are not interchangeable. It MUST begin with `rp_`.
#
# Setting this to the `app_...` ID is a silent trap: `/api/enroll/rp-context` still answers 200
# with a valid signature, and World's own `POST /api/v4/verify/{id}` accepts either form — so
# every server-side check passes. The rejection happens client-side, inside
# `idkit_wasm_bg.wasm`: `RpContextWasm`'s constructor requires an RP ID starting with `rp_` and
# otherwise throws `invalid_rp_id_format`, so the widget never opens and no biometric step is
# ever offered. Nobody can enroll, and nothing in the server logs says why. See errata E-17.
RP_ID=rp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Client-bundle mirror of WORLD_ID_ACTION below — the action name is public (it's sent in the
# IDKit request from the browser), so this is not a secret duplication.
#
# The `aval-` prefix is deliberate and survived the rename to VouchMe: the action is registered
# in the World Developer Portal, off this repo, and every nullifier ever issued derives from it.
# Renaming it would mean an unregistered action (verification fails) or a fresh namespace (every
# enrolled human could enroll again). Left as-is on purpose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLD_ID_ACTION=aval-enroll-v1

# ─── World Chain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLDCHAIN_RPC=https://worldchain-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/public

# Address Book contract — Orb anchor lookups (docs/03-worldid.md §3). Read live, never cached
# in the scoring path.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADDRESS_BOOK=0x57b930D551e677CC36e2fA036Ae2fe8FdaE0330D

# ─── src/lib/chain.ts — live World Chain Sepolia data source ───────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_MODE=live switches src/lib/mock.ts from the static fixture graph to
# src/lib/chain.ts, which reads Enrolled/Vouched/Reaffirmed/Revoked logs directly off
# VouchMeRegistry via viem — no subgraph, no indexer. Any other value (including unset) uses the
# fixture. All of the values below are REQUIRED when NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_MODE=live; chain.ts throws
# a clear error naming the missing variable rather than silently falling back to fixtures.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_MODE=fixture

# World Chain Sepolia RPC. NEXT_PUBLIC_WORLDCHAIN_RPC above is reused if set; this is the
# fallback name (matches WORLDCHAIN_SEPOLIA_RPC used by every script under scripts/ and
# contracts/.env, for one RPC value across the repo).
WORLDCHAIN_SEPOLIA_RPC=https://worldchain-sepolia.g.alchemy.com/public

# deployments/worldchain-sepolia.json is the authoritative record for every value below — copy
# from there, not from a chat transcript or a doc that might be stale.
DEPLOYMENT_BLOCK=
VOUCHME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
GENESIS_ANCHOR_BOOK_ADDRESS=
PRESENCE_DRIP_ADDRESS=
# Client-bundle mirrors — contract addresses are public, not secret. The browser needs these to
# build enroll()/vouch()/claim() calldata for the connected wallet to sign directly.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VOUCHME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRESENCE_DRIP_ADDRESS=
# Relying Party signing key for World ID `rp_context` (docs/03-worldid.md §2.1). This deployment
# currently reuses ATTESTOR_PRIVATE_KEY for this — see src/app/api/enroll/rp-context/route.ts's
# doc comment. Verify against the World Developer Portal whether a distinct RP signing key is
# actually required before relying on this in anything beyond a testnet demo.
# Optional — included in the API `meta.contracts` envelope when set, but not read from directly
# by chain.ts (no platform/report data exists on this deployment yet).
REPORT_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
PLATFORM_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
CREDIBILITY_VAULT_ADDRESS=
VOUCHME_TOKEN_ADDRESS=

# The identity the app renders as "you" (task requirement: configurable, not hardcoded). A real
# enrolled address on the live deployment — see scripts/identities.mjs for how the demo
# identities (anchor1..3, alice, bob, carol, dave, ring1..6) are derived from a fixed, public,
# non-secret seed. NOT a private key.
ME_ADDRESS=

# ─── Attestor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs EIP-712 EnrollmentAttestation / VouchAttestation (docs/03-worldid.md §2, §5).
# Local/dev only — in production this key lives in KMS and is never read from .env or
# generated client-side (docs/07-app-api.md §6, docs/03-worldid.md §7 "Signing key exposure").
ATTESTOR_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ─── Subgraph ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SUBGRAPH_URL=https://api.studio.thegraph.com/query/00000/vouchme/version/latest

# The nullifier namespace. See note above.
WORLD_ID_ACTION=aval-enroll-v1
